1
00:02:32,500 --> 00:02:34,320
The bastard of Winterfell.

2
00:02:35,380 --> 00:02:37,530
The dwarf of Casterly Rock.

3
00:02:42,930 --> 00:02:44,830
I believe we last saw each other atop the Wall.

4
00:02:45,510 --> 00:02:48,130
You were pissing off the edge if I remember right.

5
00:02:49,620 --> 00:02:51,560
Picked up some scars along the road.

6
00:02:52,440 --> 00:02:56,000
It's been a long road, but we're both still here.

7
00:02:58,230 --> 00:02:59,630
I'm Tyrion Lannister.

8
00:03:00,030 --> 00:03:03,140
- Davos Seaworth. - Ah, the Onion Knight.

9
00:03:03,350 --> 00:03:06,150
We fought on opposite sides at the Battle of Blackwater Bay.

10
00:03:06,320 --> 00:03:07,770
Unluckily for me.

11
00:03:09,960 --> 00:03:12,480
Missandei is the queen's most trusted advisor.

12
00:03:13,640 --> 00:03:15,270
Welcome to Dragonstone.

13
00:03:15,270 --> 00:03:17,060
Our queen knows it is a long journey.

14
00:03:17,060 --> 00:03:19,860
She appreciates the efforts you have made on her behalf.

15
00:03:21,060 --> 00:03:23,520
If you wouldn't mind handing over your weapons.

16
00:03:28,970 --> 00:03:29,760
Of course.

17
00:03:54,670 --> 00:03:56,590
Please, this way.

18
00:04:01,010 --> 00:04:02,000
Where are you from?

19
00:04:02,680 --> 00:04:04,460
I can't place the accent.

20
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:06,850
I was born on the Island of Naath.

21
00:04:07,860 --> 00:04:09,560
I hear it's beautiful down there.

22
00:04:09,930 --> 00:04:11,960
Palm trees and butterflies.

23
00:04:11,960 --> 00:04:13,170
Haven't been, myself.

24
00:04:17,740 --> 00:04:19,200
This place has changed.

25
00:04:25,900 --> 00:04:28,900
And Sansa? I hear she's alive and well.

26
00:04:28,900 --> 00:04:31,540
- She is. - Does she miss me terribly?

27
00:04:34,490 --> 00:04:37,030
A sham marriage. And unconsummated.

28
00:04:37,030 --> 00:04:40,030
- I didn't ask. - Well, it was. Wasn't.

29
00:04:40,030 --> 00:04:40,900
Anyway...

30
00:04:42,050 --> 00:04:43,970
she's much smarter than she lets on.

31
00:04:44,920 --> 00:04:46,470
She's starting to let on.

32
00:04:47,160 --> 00:04:47,910
Good.

33
00:04:49,490 --> 00:04:50,330
At some point,

34
00:04:50,330 --> 00:04:53,290
I want to hear how a Night's watch recruit became King in the North.

35
00:04:54,230 --> 00:04:55,910
As long as you tell me how a Lannister

36
00:04:55,910 --> 00:04:58,380
became Hand to Daenerys Targaryen.

37
00:04:58,940 --> 00:05:00,650
A long and bloody tale.

38
00:05:01,220 --> 00:05:03,580
To be honest, I was drunk for most of it.

39
00:05:06,270 --> 00:05:08,700
My bannermen think I'm a fool for coming here.

40
00:05:08,710 --> 00:05:09,800
Of course they do.

41
00:05:10,380 --> 00:05:12,790
If I was your Hand, I would have advised against it.

42
00:05:15,560 --> 00:05:16,920
General rule of thumb--

43
00:05:17,660 --> 00:05:20,240
Stark men don't fare well when they travel south.

44
00:05:20,560 --> 00:05:21,290
True...

45
00:05:22,450 --> 00:05:23,960
but I'm not a Stark.

46
00:05:38,690 --> 00:05:40,430
I'd say you get used to them...

47
00:05:42,730 --> 00:05:43,960
but you never really do.

48
00:05:47,850 --> 00:05:50,500
Come, their mother is waiting for you.

49
00:06:03,510 --> 00:06:06,180
I wondered why you weren't there to meet our guests.

50
00:06:07,650 --> 00:06:10,190
You begged us to summon the King in the North.

51
00:06:10,280 --> 00:06:11,980
Don't you want to see him again?

52
00:06:12,740 --> 00:06:14,310
I've done my part.

53
00:06:15,240 --> 00:06:17,540
I've brought ice and fire together.

54
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:19,240
Strange.

55
00:06:19,770 --> 00:06:22,180
You spoke so highly of Jon Snow,

56
00:06:22,180 --> 00:06:25,210
but when he arrives, you hide on a cliff.

57
00:06:26,080 --> 00:06:28,510
I didn't take you for a bashful girl.

58
00:06:28,980 --> 00:06:32,480
My time whispering in the ears of kings has come to an end.

59
00:06:32,480 --> 00:06:33,920
Oh, I doubt that.

60
00:06:35,110 --> 00:06:37,520
Give us common folk one taste of power,

61
00:06:37,520 --> 00:06:39,990
we're like the lion who tasted man.

62
00:06:40,560 --> 00:06:42,620
Nothing is ever so sweet again.

63
00:06:43,640 --> 00:06:46,380
Neither of us is common folk anymore.

64
00:06:49,010 --> 00:06:50,800
I did not part on good terms

65
00:06:50,810 --> 00:06:53,650
with the King in the North or his advisor.

66
00:06:53,910 --> 00:06:54,690
Why?

67
00:06:56,420 --> 00:06:58,290
Because of mistakes I made.

68
00:07:00,660 --> 00:07:02,260
Terrible mistakes.

69
00:07:04,370 --> 00:07:06,950
I would only be a distraction if I stayed.

70
00:07:07,440 --> 00:07:09,780
- So, where will you go? - Volantis.

71
00:07:09,780 --> 00:07:10,590
Good.

72
00:07:11,930 --> 00:07:13,550
If you don't mind my saying,

73
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:17,170
I don't think you should return to Westeros.

74
00:07:17,810 --> 00:07:19,850
I'm not sure you'd be safe here.

75
00:07:22,250 --> 00:07:24,790
Oh, I will return, dear Spider.

76
00:07:25,350 --> 00:07:27,110
- One last time. - My lady--

77
00:07:27,110 --> 00:07:29,420
I have to die in this strange country.

78
00:07:30,540 --> 00:07:31,680
Just like you.

79
00:08:14,960 --> 00:08:16,250
You stand in the presence

80
00:08:16,250 --> 00:08:19,070
of Daenerys Stormborn of House Targaryen,

81
00:08:19,080 --> 00:08:21,280
rightful heir to the Iron Throne,

82
00:08:21,320 --> 00:08:24,090
rightful Queen of the Andals and the First Men,

83
00:08:24,190 --> 00:08:26,390
Protector of the Seven Kingdoms,

84
00:08:26,450 --> 00:08:28,240
the Mother of Dragons,

85
00:08:28,260 --> 00:08:30,610
the Khaleesi of the Great Grass Sea,

86
00:08:30,610 --> 00:08:34,160
the Unburnt, the Breaker of Chains.

87
00:08:39,460 --> 00:08:40,880
This is Jon Snow.

88
00:08:45,120 --> 00:08:46,500
He's King in the North.

89
00:08:49,920 --> 00:08:52,040
Thank you for traveling so far, my lord.

90
00:08:52,460 --> 00:08:54,160
I hope the seas weren't too rough.

91
00:08:54,160 --> 00:08:55,590
The winds were kind, Your Grace.

92
00:08:55,590 --> 00:08:59,400
Apologies, I have a Flea Bottom accent, I know,

93
00:08:59,730 --> 00:09:02,500
but Jon Snow is King in the North, Your Grace.

94
00:09:02,500 --> 00:09:04,370
- He's not a lord. - Forgive me--

95
00:09:04,370 --> 00:09:06,890
Your Grace, this is Ser Davos Seaworth.

96
00:09:07,070 --> 00:09:08,720
Forgive me, Ser Davos.

97
00:09:08,780 --> 00:09:11,100
I never did receive a formal education,

98
00:09:11,100 --> 00:09:12,320
but I could have sworn I read

99
00:09:12,320 --> 00:09:15,830
the last King in the North was Torrhen Stark,

100
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:18,860
who bent the knee to my ancestor, Aegon Targaryen.

101
00:09:18,990 --> 00:09:22,290
In exchange for his life and the lives of the Northmen,

102
00:09:22,300 --> 00:09:26,810
Torrhen Stark swore fealty to House Targaryen in perpetuity.

103
00:09:27,360 --> 00:09:28,880
Or do I have my facts wrong?

104
00:09:29,730 --> 00:09:31,030
I wasn't there, Your Grace.

105
00:09:31,030 --> 00:09:33,220
No, of course not.

106
00:09:33,510 --> 00:09:36,120
But still, an oath is an oath.

107
00:09:36,470 --> 00:09:38,160
And perpetuity means--

108
00:09:38,440 --> 00:09:40,800
what does perpetuity mean, Lord Tyrion?

109
00:09:41,210 --> 00:09:42,090
Forever.

110
00:09:43,280 --> 00:09:44,190
Forever.

111
00:09:45,140 --> 00:09:47,410
So I assume, my lord...

112
00:09:47,410 --> 00:09:49,270
...you're here to bend the knee.

113
00:09:51,990 --> 00:09:53,210
I am not.

114
00:09:56,820 --> 00:09:58,440
Well, that is unfortunate.

115
00:10:00,030 --> 00:10:01,570
You've traveled all this way

116
00:10:01,570 --> 00:10:03,690
to break faith with House Targaryen?

117
00:10:03,690 --> 00:10:04,810
Break faith?

118
00:10:06,400 --> 00:10:08,510
Your father burned my grandfather alive.

119
00:10:08,510 --> 00:10:10,140
He burned my uncle alive.

120
00:10:10,610 --> 00:10:11,580
He would have burned the Seven Kingdoms--

121
00:10:11,580 --> 00:10:14,940
My father... was an evil man.

122
00:10:16,660 --> 00:10:18,610
On behalf of House Targaryen...

123
00:10:20,100 --> 00:10:21,620
I ask your forgiveness

124
00:10:21,620 --> 00:10:24,270
for the crimes he committed against your family.

125
00:10:24,670 --> 00:10:27,390
And I ask you not to judge a daughter

126
00:10:27,390 --> 00:10:29,220
by the sins of her father.

127
00:10:31,250 --> 00:10:34,800
Our two houses were allies for centuries,

128
00:10:34,990 --> 00:10:36,630
and those were the best centuries

129
00:10:36,630 --> 00:10:38,640
the Seven Kingdoms have ever known.

130
00:10:38,650 --> 00:10:41,180
Centuries of peace and prosperity

131
00:10:41,420 --> 00:10:44,040
with a Targaryen sitting on the Iron Throne

132
00:10:44,190 --> 00:10:47,510
and a Stark serving as Warden of the North.

133
00:10:48,470 --> 00:10:50,820
I am the last Targaryen, Jon Snow.

134
00:10:52,150 --> 00:10:54,690
Honor the pledge your ancestor made to mine.

135
00:10:54,840 --> 00:10:57,980
Bend the knee and I will name you Warden of the North.

136
00:10:58,040 --> 00:11:01,950
Together, we will save this country from those who would destroy it.

137
00:11:12,770 --> 00:11:13,560
You're right.

138
00:11:14,910 --> 00:11:17,380
You're not guilty of your father's crimes.

139
00:11:17,680 --> 00:11:20,620
And I'm not beholden to my ancestor's vows.

140
00:11:22,190 --> 00:11:23,500
Then why are you here?

141
00:11:24,270 --> 00:11:27,430
Because I need your help, and you need mine.

142
00:11:30,300 --> 00:11:34,100
Did you see three dragons flying overhead when you arrived?

143
00:11:34,270 --> 00:11:35,060
I did.

144
00:11:35,060 --> 00:11:37,090
And did you see the Dothraki,

145
00:11:37,500 --> 00:11:39,870
all of whom have sworn to kill for me?

146
00:11:39,870 --> 00:11:41,250
They're hard to miss.

147
00:11:41,250 --> 00:11:44,110
But still, I need your help?

148
00:11:44,110 --> 00:11:45,750
Not to defeat Cersei.

149
00:11:45,790 --> 00:11:48,840
You could storm King's Landing tomorrow and the city would fall.

150
00:11:48,960 --> 00:11:50,610
Hell, we almost took it

151
00:11:50,610 --> 00:11:51,600
and we didn't even have dragons.

152
00:11:51,600 --> 00:11:54,760
- Almost. - But you haven't stormed King's Landing.

153
00:11:55,530 --> 00:11:56,310
Why not?

154
00:11:57,510 --> 00:11:58,700
The only reason I can see

155
00:11:58,700 --> 00:12:01,300
is you don't want to kill thousands of innocent people.

156
00:12:01,310 --> 00:12:02,840
It's the fastest way to win the war,

157
00:12:02,840 --> 00:12:04,330
but you won't do it,

158
00:12:04,600 --> 00:12:07,720
which means, at the very least,

159
00:12:08,140 --> 00:12:09,560
you're better than Cersei.

160
00:12:11,040 --> 00:12:13,720
Still, that doesn't explain why I need your help.

161
00:12:16,330 --> 00:12:20,270
Because right now, you and I and Cersei and everyone else,

162
00:12:20,920 --> 00:12:22,430
we're children playing at a game,

163
00:12:22,430 --> 00:12:24,510
screaming that the rules aren't fair.

164
00:12:24,510 --> 00:12:26,690
- You told me you liked this man. - I do.

165
00:12:26,690 --> 00:12:30,180
In the time since he's met me, he's refused to call me queen,

166
00:12:30,180 --> 00:12:33,080
he's refused to bow, and now he's calling me a child.

167
00:12:33,080 --> 00:12:37,170
I believe he's calling all of us children. Figure of speech.

168
00:12:37,170 --> 00:12:40,160
Your Grace, everyone you know will die before winter's over

169
00:12:40,160 --> 00:12:42,330
if we don't defeat the enemy to the north.

170
00:12:42,330 --> 00:12:44,810
As far as I can see, you are the enemy to the north.

171
00:12:44,810 --> 00:12:46,260
I am not your enemy.

172
00:12:48,190 --> 00:12:50,050
The dead are the enemy.

173
00:12:50,380 --> 00:12:51,530
The dead?

174
00:12:52,850 --> 00:12:54,290
Is that another figure of speech?

175
00:12:54,290 --> 00:12:55,950
The Army of the Dead is on the march.

176
00:12:55,950 --> 00:12:57,710
The Army of the Dead?

177
00:12:58,940 --> 00:13:00,320
You don't know me well, my lord,

178
00:13:00,320 --> 00:13:03,610
but do you think I'm a liar or a madman?

179
00:13:03,610 --> 00:13:06,080
No, I don't think you're either of those things.

180
00:13:06,080 --> 00:13:08,090
The Army of the Dead is real.

181
00:13:08,410 --> 00:13:09,690
The white walkers are real.

182
00:13:09,690 --> 00:13:12,130
The Night King is real. I've seen them.

183
00:13:12,610 --> 00:13:14,130
If they get past the Wall

184
00:13:14,130 --> 00:13:16,860
and we're squabbling amongst ourselves...

185
00:13:19,550 --> 00:13:20,670
we're finished.

186
00:13:26,850 --> 00:13:28,970
I was born at Dragonstone.

187
00:13:30,830 --> 00:13:32,460
Not that I can remember it.

188
00:13:33,660 --> 00:13:36,660
We fled before Robert's assassins could find us.

189
00:13:36,990 --> 00:13:39,960
Robert was your father's best friend, no?

190
00:13:40,370 --> 00:13:44,060
I wonder if your father knew his best friend sent assassins

191
00:13:44,060 --> 00:13:46,490
to murder a baby girl in her crib.

192
00:13:48,210 --> 00:13:50,040
Not that it matters now, of course.

193
00:13:51,490 --> 00:13:54,320
I spent my life in foreign lands.

194
00:13:54,600 --> 00:13:57,180
So many men have tried to kill me,

195
00:13:57,620 --> 00:13:59,350
I don't remember all their names.

196
00:14:00,990 --> 00:14:04,460
I have been sold like a broodmare.

197
00:14:05,190 --> 00:14:08,100
I've been chained and betrayed,

198
00:14:08,560 --> 00:14:11,470
raped and defiled.

199
00:14:11,470 --> 00:14:13,680
Do you know what kept me standing

200
00:14:13,690 --> 00:14:15,630
through all those years in exile?

201
00:14:17,060 --> 00:14:18,180
Faith.

202
00:14:19,520 --> 00:14:21,160
Not in any gods,

203
00:14:21,890 --> 00:14:24,770
not in myths and legends.

204
00:14:25,260 --> 00:14:27,020
In myself.

205
00:14:27,870 --> 00:14:30,480
In Daenerys Targaryen.

206
00:14:31,690 --> 00:14:34,600
The world hadn't seen a dragon in centuries

207
00:14:34,600 --> 00:14:36,510
until my children were born.

208
00:14:37,160 --> 00:14:40,920
The Dothraki hadn't crossed the sea, any sea.

209
00:14:41,820 --> 00:14:43,560
They did for me.

210
00:14:44,550 --> 00:14:47,380
I was born to rule the Seven Kingdoms,

211
00:14:48,550 --> 00:14:49,980
and I will.

212
00:14:53,070 --> 00:14:55,200
You'll be ruling over a graveyard

213
00:14:55,760 --> 00:14:57,810
if we don't defeat the Night King.

214
00:14:59,580 --> 00:15:02,650
The war against my sister has already begun.

215
00:15:02,650 --> 00:15:06,200
You can't expect us to halt hostilities and join you in fighting

216
00:15:06,800 --> 00:15:08,450
whatever you saw beyond the Wall.

217
00:15:11,070 --> 00:15:12,230
You don't believe him.

218
00:15:12,660 --> 00:15:15,170
I understand that. It sounds like nonsense.

219
00:15:15,790 --> 00:15:16,800
But if destiny has brought

220
00:15:16,810 --> 00:15:19,270
Daenerys Targaryen back to our shores,

221
00:15:19,540 --> 00:15:22,370
it has also made Jon Snow King in the North.

222
00:15:22,990 --> 00:15:25,320
You were the first to bring Dothraki to Westeros?

223
00:15:25,960 --> 00:15:29,130
He is the first to make allies of wildlings and Northmen.

224
00:15:29,130 --> 00:15:31,140
He was named Lord Commander of the Night's Watch.

225
00:15:31,140 --> 00:15:32,420
He was named King in the North.

226
00:15:32,430 --> 00:15:33,520
Not because of his birthright.

227
00:15:33,520 --> 00:15:36,080
He has no birthright. He's a damn bastard.

228
00:15:36,390 --> 00:15:39,810
All those hard sons of bitches chose him as their leader

229
00:15:41,190 --> 00:15:42,990
because they believe in him.

230
00:15:44,180 --> 00:15:46,050
All those things you don't believe in,

231
00:15:46,120 --> 00:15:47,740
he faced those things.

232
00:15:47,760 --> 00:15:50,130
He fought those things for the good of his people.

233
00:15:50,130 --> 00:15:51,490
He risked his life for his people.

234
00:15:51,490 --> 00:15:53,180
He took a knife in the heart for his people.

235
00:15:53,180 --> 00:15:54,400
He gave his own--

236
00:16:01,240 --> 00:16:03,800
If we don't put aside our enmities and band together,

237
00:16:03,800 --> 00:16:04,870
we will die.

238
00:16:06,180 --> 00:16:09,710
And then it doesn't matter whose skeleton sits on the Iron Throne.

239
00:16:09,710 --> 00:16:12,210
If it doesn't matter, then you might as well kneel.

240
00:16:12,250 --> 00:16:14,200
Swear your allegiance to Queen Daenerys,

241
00:16:14,200 --> 00:16:15,860
help her to defeat my sister,

242
00:16:15,860 --> 00:16:17,520
and together, our armies will protect the North.

243
00:16:17,520 --> 00:16:19,180
There's no time for that.

244
00:16:20,040 --> 00:16:21,620
There's no time for any of this!

245
00:16:21,620 --> 00:16:23,200
While we stand here, debating--

246
00:16:23,200 --> 00:16:25,310
It takes no time to bend the knee.

247
00:16:25,340 --> 00:16:26,850
Pledge your sword to her cause.

248
00:16:26,850 --> 00:16:28,220
And why would I do that?

249
00:16:31,620 --> 00:16:33,880
I mean no offense, Your Grace,

250
00:16:33,880 --> 00:16:35,190
but I don't know you.

251
00:16:35,660 --> 00:16:36,900
As far as I can tell,

252
00:16:36,900 --> 00:16:40,050
your claim to the throne rests entirely on your father's name,

253
00:16:40,050 --> 00:16:43,230
and my own father fought to overthrow the Mad King.

254
00:16:45,270 --> 00:16:46,720
The lords of the North

255
00:16:47,190 --> 00:16:49,820
placed their trust in me to lead them,

256
00:16:50,140 --> 00:16:53,770
and I will continue to do so as well as I can.

257
00:16:55,340 --> 00:16:56,290
That's fair.

258
00:16:58,290 --> 00:17:00,150
It's also fair to point out

259
00:17:00,160 --> 00:17:03,450
that I'm the rightful Queen of the Seven Kingdoms.

260
00:17:04,330 --> 00:17:07,730
By declaring yourself king of the northernmost kingdom,

261
00:17:08,040 --> 00:17:09,980
you are in open rebellion.

262
00:17:20,370 --> 00:17:22,280
Your Grace, please dismiss your guests.

263
00:17:22,450 --> 00:17:23,740
I have grave news.

264
00:17:26,810 --> 00:17:28,330
You must forgive my manners.

265
00:17:28,830 --> 00:17:30,910
You'll both be tired after your long journey.

266
00:17:31,280 --> 00:17:33,870
We'll have baths drawn for you and supper sent to your rooms.

267
00:17:43,150 --> 00:17:44,440
Am I your prisoner?

268
00:17:48,570 --> 00:17:49,770
Not yet.

269
00:18:07,390 --> 00:18:10,870
Our ironborn and Dornish allies were attacked en route to Dorne.

270
00:18:10,870 --> 00:18:13,070
- And? - Two or three ships escaped,

271
00:18:13,070 --> 00:18:15,220
the rest, sunk or captured.

272
00:18:15,500 --> 00:18:17,930
Ellaria and the Sand Snakes, dead or captured.

273
00:18:17,930 --> 00:18:20,330
The Greyjoys, dead or captured.

274
00:18:21,210 --> 00:18:22,070
All of them?

275
00:18:23,630 --> 00:18:27,080
- Pull! - Heave!

276
00:18:27,150 --> 00:18:28,340
Pull!

277
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:40,270
Your sister's dead?

278
00:18:41,800 --> 00:18:43,070
Euron has her.

279
00:18:44,200 --> 00:18:45,640
You saw him take her?

280
00:18:47,590 --> 00:18:50,500
- But you got away? - I couldn't save her.

281
00:18:50,970 --> 00:18:51,940
I tried.

282
00:18:53,890 --> 00:18:55,790
You wouldn't be here if you tried.

283
00:19:00,350 --> 00:19:01,540
Come, men!

284
00:19:01,960 --> 00:19:02,930
Sails up!

285
00:19:12,180 --> 00:19:13,570
Murderer!

286
00:19:24,880 --> 00:19:26,390
Whores!

287
00:19:27,970 --> 00:19:28,990
Traitor!

288
00:19:33,150 --> 00:19:34,530
This is the life.

289
00:19:35,660 --> 00:19:39,600
Look at them, cheering for a Greyjoy.

290
00:19:43,470 --> 00:19:44,920
I have to be honest,

291
00:19:45,630 --> 00:19:47,260
this is making me hard.

292
00:19:50,190 --> 00:19:53,660
Did you see Little Theon's face right before he jumped overboard?

293
00:19:54,260 --> 00:19:56,050
"Oh, no!"

294
00:19:56,910 --> 00:19:58,090
What a twat.

295
00:20:26,080 --> 00:20:29,440
- Whore! Whore! Whore! - Murderers!

296
00:21:02,290 --> 00:21:05,630
My queen, please accept this gift

297
00:21:05,630 --> 00:21:09,700
on behalf of all of your loyal subjects in the Iron Islands.

298
00:21:14,580 --> 00:21:17,900
I give you what no other man could give--

299
00:21:19,230 --> 00:21:20,370
justice.

300
00:21:21,720 --> 00:21:24,220
Justice for your murdered daughter.

301
00:21:34,190 --> 00:21:37,990
You've proven yourself the greatest captain on the fourteen seas

302
00:21:38,310 --> 00:21:40,130
and a true friend to the crown.

303
00:21:41,730 --> 00:21:43,930
You deserve more than a true friend.

304
00:21:44,580 --> 00:21:47,390
And you deserve a proper reward for your heroism.

305
00:21:47,620 --> 00:21:49,730
There's only one reward I want.

306
00:21:51,340 --> 00:21:53,890
You shall have what your heart desires...

307
00:21:56,020 --> 00:21:57,270
when the war is won.

308
00:22:04,220 --> 00:22:07,670
With Euron Greyjoy commanding our naval forces

309
00:22:07,830 --> 00:22:10,240
and Jaime Lannister leading our armies,

310
00:22:10,540 --> 00:22:12,570
the sons and daughters of Westeros

311
00:22:12,580 --> 00:22:14,240
shall defend our country.

312
00:22:21,470 --> 00:22:23,560
There's nothing quite like it, is there?

313
00:22:24,090 --> 00:22:25,520
The love of the people.

314
00:22:25,930 --> 00:22:27,610
Though I suppose you wouldn't know.

315
00:22:28,370 --> 00:22:31,470
This same mob spat at my sister not long ago.

316
00:22:31,710 --> 00:22:33,110
And if you turn on us,

317
00:22:33,110 --> 00:22:36,390
they'll cheer to see your head mounted on a spike.

318
00:22:36,470 --> 00:22:37,540
Or yours.

319
00:22:37,940 --> 00:22:40,030
They just like severed heads, really.

320
00:22:40,890 --> 00:22:44,080
Listen, if you have any advice at all,

321
00:22:44,080 --> 00:22:45,610
I would love to hear it.

322
00:22:45,890 --> 00:22:49,060
When we have an hour or two to speak as brothers.

323
00:22:49,060 --> 00:22:50,130
Advice?

324
00:22:50,860 --> 00:22:53,750
Does she like it gentle or rough?

325
00:22:54,330 --> 00:22:56,160
A finger in the bum?

326
00:22:56,850 --> 00:22:59,180
Not now. We'll talk later.

327
00:23:16,990 --> 00:23:19,160
I want you to know I understand.

328
00:23:20,160 --> 00:23:21,430
Even though we're enemies, you and I,

329
00:23:21,440 --> 00:23:23,580
I understand the fury that drives you.

330
00:23:24,560 --> 00:23:26,360
I was there that day when Ser Gregor

331
00:23:26,360 --> 00:23:28,000
crushed your lover's head.

332
00:23:30,020 --> 00:23:31,770
If I close my eyes,

333
00:23:32,650 --> 00:23:35,330
I can hear the sound of Oberyn's skull breaking.

334
00:23:35,330 --> 00:23:36,910
The sound of your scream.

335
00:23:37,620 --> 00:23:39,140
I never heard a sound like that.

336
00:23:39,140 --> 00:23:41,160
I thought, "That's true love."

337
00:23:42,720 --> 00:23:45,080
Oberyn looked beautiful that day. He really did.

338
00:23:45,080 --> 00:23:46,150
No one moved like him.

339
00:23:46,150 --> 00:23:48,430
No one had such skill with a spear.

340
00:23:49,580 --> 00:23:51,300
Even Ser Gregor couldn't stop him.

341
00:23:52,720 --> 00:23:54,930
If only he hadn't taunted him.

342
00:23:55,380 --> 00:23:58,450
He could've walked away and left poor Ser Gregor to die.

343
00:23:58,760 --> 00:24:00,630
But that wasn't your lover's way, was it?

344
00:24:01,820 --> 00:24:03,260
Now he's buried somewhere.

345
00:24:04,080 --> 00:24:06,080
And here's Ser Gregor, stronger than ever.

346
00:24:06,750 --> 00:24:08,260
That must be difficult for you.

347
00:24:12,410 --> 00:24:14,230
When my daughter was taken from me,

348
00:24:14,230 --> 00:24:15,880
my only daughter...

349
00:24:17,640 --> 00:24:20,230
well, you can't imagine how that feels

350
00:24:20,230 --> 00:24:22,020
unless you've lost a child.

351
00:24:23,230 --> 00:24:25,140
I fed her at my own breast even though they told me

352
00:24:25,150 --> 00:24:26,860
to give her to the wet nurse.

353
00:24:28,120 --> 00:24:30,460
I couldn't bear to see her in another woman's arms.

354
00:24:31,640 --> 00:24:33,180
I never got to have a mother,

355
00:24:33,790 --> 00:24:35,100
but Myrcella did.

356
00:24:35,260 --> 00:24:38,890
She was mine, and you took her from me.

357
00:24:38,900 --> 00:24:40,260
Why did you do that?

358
00:24:47,480 --> 00:24:48,590
Doesn't matter now.

359
00:24:57,310 --> 00:24:58,920
Your daughter's a beauty, too.

360
00:25:00,440 --> 00:25:01,700
Those brown eyes.

361
00:25:03,010 --> 00:25:04,040
Those lips.

362
00:25:06,140 --> 00:25:07,860
Perfect Dornish beauty.

363
00:25:08,830 --> 00:25:10,410
I imagine she's your favorite.

364
00:25:10,410 --> 00:25:13,150
I know, I know, we're not supposed to have favorites,

365
00:25:13,430 --> 00:25:15,030
but still, we're only human.

366
00:25:16,900 --> 00:25:18,260
We love whom we love.

367
00:25:21,480 --> 00:25:23,660
I'm sorry, I can't understand you.

368
00:25:24,050 --> 00:25:26,670
That gag makes it impossible to understand what you're saying.

369
00:25:26,670 --> 00:25:28,090
It must be frustrating.

370
00:25:31,760 --> 00:25:33,270
We all make our choices.

371
00:25:34,730 --> 00:25:36,410
You chose to murder my daughter.

372
00:25:37,290 --> 00:25:39,790
You must have felt powerful after you made that choice.

373
00:25:40,340 --> 00:25:41,630
Do you feel powerful now?

374
00:25:48,330 --> 00:25:49,550
I don't sleep very well.

375
00:25:50,520 --> 00:25:51,850
Not at all, really.

376
00:25:51,860 --> 00:25:53,810
I lie in bed and I stare at the canopy

377
00:25:53,810 --> 00:25:56,180
and imagine ways of killing my enemies.

378
00:25:56,650 --> 00:25:57,920
How to destroy Ellaria Sand,

379
00:25:57,920 --> 00:26:00,250
the woman who murdered my only daughter.

380
00:26:01,640 --> 00:26:03,650
I thought about having Ser Gregor crush your skull

381
00:26:03,650 --> 00:26:05,110
the way he did Oberyn's.

382
00:26:05,460 --> 00:26:08,630
It would be poetic, I suppose, but fast, too fast.

383
00:26:10,230 --> 00:26:12,730
I thought about having him crush your daughter's skull.

384
00:26:14,070 --> 00:26:15,730
She's so beautiful.

385
00:26:17,160 --> 00:26:18,910
The thought of this lovely face

386
00:26:18,910 --> 00:26:20,810
cracking open like a duck egg,

387
00:26:21,220 --> 00:26:22,840
no, it's just not right.

388
00:26:30,430 --> 00:26:31,400
Mama.

389
00:26:42,040 --> 00:26:44,060
Qyburn here is the cleverest man I know.

390
00:26:44,640 --> 00:26:47,670
Clever enough to learn what poison you used to murder Myrcella.

391
00:26:47,940 --> 00:26:48,960
The Long Goodbye, was that it?

392
00:26:48,960 --> 00:26:51,510
- The Long Farewell. - That's the one.

393
00:26:55,530 --> 00:26:57,240
How long does the poison take?

394
00:26:57,300 --> 00:26:59,490
Difficult to say-- hours, days.

395
00:26:59,490 --> 00:27:01,590
It depends on the subject's constitution.

396
00:27:01,590 --> 00:27:02,900
But death is certain?

397
00:27:02,900 --> 00:27:05,050
Oh, yes, Your Grace, quite certain.

398
00:27:10,580 --> 00:27:12,490
Your daughter will die here in this cell,

399
00:27:13,410 --> 00:27:15,480
and you will be here watching when she does.

400
00:27:17,140 --> 00:27:19,210
You'll be here the rest of your days.

401
00:27:21,110 --> 00:27:23,960
If you refuse to eat, we'll force food down your throat.

402
00:27:25,130 --> 00:27:27,930
You will live to watch your daughter rot.

403
00:27:29,040 --> 00:27:31,810
To watch that beautiful face collapse...

404
00:27:31,820 --> 00:27:33,810
...to bone and dust.

405
00:27:36,540 --> 00:27:39,040
All the while contemplating the choices you've made.

406
00:27:42,570 --> 00:27:45,080
Make sure the guards change the torches every few hours.

407
00:27:45,080 --> 00:27:46,740
I don't want her to miss a thing.

408
00:28:17,470 --> 00:28:18,250
No.

409
00:29:01,040 --> 00:29:02,080
Don't.

410
00:29:14,140 --> 00:29:17,030
What are you doing? No one can see us like this.

411
00:29:17,030 --> 00:29:20,180
I am the Queen of the Seven Kingdoms. I'll do as I please.

412
00:29:26,410 --> 00:29:27,490
Forgive me, Your Grace.

413
00:29:27,500 --> 00:29:29,490
The visitor from Braavos has arrived.

414
00:29:29,670 --> 00:29:32,420
Good. And we'll need fresh sheets for the bed.

415
00:29:32,440 --> 00:29:33,640
At once, Your Grace.

416
00:29:44,660 --> 00:29:45,790
No, thank you.

417
00:29:47,400 --> 00:29:49,000
My condolences, Your Grace,

418
00:29:49,000 --> 00:29:50,930
on the death of your son.

419
00:29:50,930 --> 00:29:53,800
From all reports, he was a fine young man.

420
00:29:53,810 --> 00:29:56,580
The Iron Bank didn't send you here to offer condolences.

421
00:29:56,770 --> 00:29:59,710
Condolences and congratulations.

422
00:29:59,930 --> 00:30:02,730
To become the first ruling Queen of the Seven Kingdoms,

423
00:30:02,730 --> 00:30:04,590
that's quite an accomplishment.

424
00:30:04,820 --> 00:30:05,970
The Iron Bank appreciates

425
00:30:05,970 --> 00:30:08,710
how you cast off the yoke of superstition,

426
00:30:08,710 --> 00:30:10,090
freeing the crown from elements

427
00:30:10,090 --> 00:30:12,720
who sought to subvert the rule of law.

428
00:30:12,720 --> 00:30:15,970
The destruction of the Sept of Baelor was a tragic accident.

429
00:30:16,070 --> 00:30:20,150
Indeed, but sometimes tragedies are necessary

430
00:30:20,150 --> 00:30:22,430
to restore order and rational leadership.

431
00:30:22,430 --> 00:30:24,310
The Iron Bank wants its gold back.

432
00:30:25,160 --> 00:30:27,600
Your father never minced words either.

433
00:30:27,840 --> 00:30:30,530
But, yes, your debts are considerable.

434
00:30:31,660 --> 00:30:34,520
And you're now engaged in a conflict on several fronts.

435
00:30:34,520 --> 00:30:37,360
We both know how expensive war can be.

436
00:30:37,360 --> 00:30:39,630
And we both know gold wins wars.

437
00:30:39,640 --> 00:30:41,110
Your vaults are empty.

438
00:30:41,120 --> 00:30:43,870
Your late husband's profligacy saw to that.

439
00:30:44,210 --> 00:30:46,840
Your wealthiest allies, the Tyrells, are now your enemies.

440
00:30:46,840 --> 00:30:50,450
You are surrounded on all sides by rivals for the throne.

441
00:30:50,450 --> 00:30:52,440
And the Iron Bank wants to bet on a winner.

442
00:30:52,440 --> 00:30:53,940
We don't make bets.

443
00:30:54,290 --> 00:30:57,560
We invest in endeavors we deem likely to be successful.

444
00:30:57,560 --> 00:30:59,650
A fancy way of saying "Bet."

445
00:31:00,730 --> 00:31:03,570
The war's already begun. I've drawn first blood.

446
00:31:04,450 --> 00:31:06,690
I decapitated the Dornish snake.

447
00:31:07,610 --> 00:31:09,360
My armada owns the Narrow Sea.

448
00:31:09,360 --> 00:31:11,740
Euron Greyjoy's armada owns the Narrow Sea.

449
00:31:11,740 --> 00:31:13,290
Euron Greyjoy is loyal to me.

450
00:31:13,290 --> 00:31:14,530
For now.

451
00:31:15,770 --> 00:31:19,560
Daenerys Targaryen has three full-grown dragons.

452
00:31:19,570 --> 00:31:23,990
How well do wooden ships fare against fire-breathing dragons?

453
00:31:24,250 --> 00:31:27,700
Her dragons might not be as invulnerable as some think.

454
00:31:28,920 --> 00:31:31,130
But let's talk about the Targaryen girl.

455
00:31:31,130 --> 00:31:33,150
You want to invest in her?

456
00:31:33,520 --> 00:31:34,810
I'm guessing the Iron Bank

457
00:31:34,810 --> 00:31:37,270
invested considerable gold in the slave trade.

458
00:31:37,270 --> 00:31:38,700
How are your profits

459
00:31:39,640 --> 00:31:41,940
now that Daenerys has freed all the slaves?

460
00:31:42,780 --> 00:31:46,100
The slave trade has entered a downturn, it's true.

461
00:31:46,280 --> 00:31:48,260
From what I gather, she considers herself

462
00:31:48,260 --> 00:31:50,690
more of a revolutionary than a monarch.

463
00:31:51,750 --> 00:31:53,190
In your experience,

464
00:31:53,200 --> 00:31:55,880
how do bankers usually fare with revolutionaries?

465
00:31:55,920 --> 00:31:58,280
The Lannisters owe the Iron Bank quite a lot of money,

466
00:31:58,280 --> 00:32:00,570
but Lannisters always pay their debts.

467
00:32:00,670 --> 00:32:04,500
Do former slaves or Dothraki or dragons?

468
00:32:08,520 --> 00:32:10,610
Your father's daughter, indeed.

469
00:32:10,610 --> 00:32:11,970
Give me a fortnight.

470
00:32:11,970 --> 00:32:14,320
Stay in King's Landing as my honored guest.

471
00:32:14,320 --> 00:32:15,560
And when you return to Braavos,

472
00:32:15,560 --> 00:32:19,780
I swear to you, my debt will be paid in full.

473
00:32:43,780 --> 00:32:45,690
I came down here to brood over my failure

474
00:32:45,690 --> 00:32:47,430
to predict the Greyjoy attack.

475
00:32:50,290 --> 00:32:51,750
You're making it difficult.

476
00:32:52,420 --> 00:32:54,700
You look a lot better brooding than I do.

477
00:32:56,950 --> 00:32:59,460
You make me feel like I'm failing at brooding over failing.

478
00:32:59,460 --> 00:33:01,320
I'm a prisoner on this island.

479
00:33:02,070 --> 00:33:04,600
I wouldn't say you're a prisoner on this island.

480
00:33:05,590 --> 00:33:06,960
You're free to walk the castle,

481
00:33:06,960 --> 00:33:08,530
the beaches, to go wherever you want.

482
00:33:08,530 --> 00:33:09,830
Except to my ship.

483
00:33:10,990 --> 00:33:12,170
You took my ship.

484
00:33:12,180 --> 00:33:14,190
I wouldn't say we took your ship.

485
00:33:14,190 --> 00:33:16,080
I'm not playing word games with you.

486
00:33:16,690 --> 00:33:18,620
The dead are coming for us all.

487
00:33:18,700 --> 00:33:19,870
Why don't you figure out what to do

488
00:33:19,870 --> 00:33:22,350
about my missing fleet and murdered allies,

489
00:33:22,460 --> 00:33:25,110
and I'll figure out what to do about your walking dead men.

490
00:33:25,110 --> 00:33:27,570
It's hard for me to fathom. It really is.

491
00:33:27,610 --> 00:33:30,610
If someone told me about the white walkers and the Night King...

492
00:33:37,900 --> 00:33:39,310
You probably don't believe me.

493
00:33:41,550 --> 00:33:42,960
I do, actually.

494
00:33:43,740 --> 00:33:44,850
You didn't before.

495
00:33:47,110 --> 00:33:49,040
"Grumkins and snarks," You called them.

496
00:33:49,040 --> 00:33:50,030
Do you remember?

497
00:33:51,310 --> 00:33:53,070
You said it was all nonsense.

498
00:33:53,430 --> 00:33:56,070
It was nonsense. Everybody knew it.

499
00:33:57,500 --> 00:33:59,200
But then Mormont saw them

500
00:33:59,520 --> 00:34:00,660
and you saw them.

501
00:34:01,080 --> 00:34:02,700
And I trust the eyes of an honest man

502
00:34:02,700 --> 00:34:04,580
more than I trust what everybody knows.

503
00:34:05,990 --> 00:34:08,140
How do I convince people who don't know me

504
00:34:08,390 --> 00:34:11,260
that an enemy they don't believe in is coming to kill them all?

505
00:34:11,950 --> 00:34:14,360
- Good question. - I know it's a good question.

506
00:34:14,360 --> 00:34:15,810
I'm looking for an answer.

507
00:34:16,780 --> 00:34:19,780
People's minds aren't made for problems that large.

508
00:34:21,080 --> 00:34:22,940
White walkers, the Night King,

509
00:34:23,450 --> 00:34:24,740
Army of the Dead--

510
00:34:25,490 --> 00:34:26,980
it's almost a relief to confront

511
00:34:26,980 --> 00:34:29,720
a comfortable, familiar monster like my sister.

512
00:34:32,400 --> 00:34:34,950
I need to help prepare my people for what's coming.

513
00:34:37,020 --> 00:34:38,770
I can't help them from here.

514
00:34:40,820 --> 00:34:42,200
I'd like to leave.

515
00:34:43,380 --> 00:34:45,780
It seems unlikely that you became King in the North

516
00:34:45,780 --> 00:34:47,280
by giving up that easily.

517
00:34:49,840 --> 00:34:52,740
Everyone told me to learn from my father's mistakes.

518
00:34:52,750 --> 00:34:53,980
Don't go south.

519
00:34:54,700 --> 00:34:57,280
Don't answer a summons from the Mad King's daughter,

520
00:34:57,280 --> 00:34:58,650
a foreign invader.

521
00:35:01,130 --> 00:35:02,210
And here I am,

522
00:35:03,770 --> 00:35:05,320
a Northern fool.

523
00:35:05,390 --> 00:35:07,170
Children are not their fathers,

524
00:35:07,870 --> 00:35:09,280
luckily for all of us.

525
00:35:11,100 --> 00:35:13,250
And sometimes there's more to foreign invaders

526
00:35:13,250 --> 00:35:15,620
and Northern fools than meets the eye.

527
00:35:16,560 --> 00:35:18,540
Daenerys could have sailed for Westeros long ago,

528
00:35:18,540 --> 00:35:19,560
but she didn't.

529
00:35:19,560 --> 00:35:21,420
Instead, she stayed where she was

530
00:35:21,420 --> 00:35:24,010
and saved many people from horrible fates,

531
00:35:24,260 --> 00:35:26,710
some of whom are on this island with us right now.

532
00:35:27,150 --> 00:35:28,230
While you're our guest here,

533
00:35:28,230 --> 00:35:29,480
you might consider asking them

534
00:35:29,480 --> 00:35:31,680
what they think of the Mad King's daughter.

535
00:35:33,060 --> 00:35:34,970
She protects people from monsters,

536
00:35:35,540 --> 00:35:36,670
just as you do.

537
00:35:37,090 --> 00:35:38,240
It's why she came here.

538
00:35:39,630 --> 00:35:40,920
And she's not about to head north

539
00:35:40,920 --> 00:35:42,440
to fight an enemy she's never seen

540
00:35:42,450 --> 00:35:44,480
on the word of a man she doesn't know.

541
00:35:44,860 --> 00:35:46,260
After a single meeting,

542
00:35:47,460 --> 00:35:49,360
it's not a reasonable thing to ask.

543
00:35:56,550 --> 00:35:58,790
So, do you have anything reasonable to ask?

544
00:36:03,430 --> 00:36:04,340
What do you mean?

545
00:36:04,740 --> 00:36:06,330
Maybe you are a Northern fool.

546
00:36:07,120 --> 00:36:10,360
I'm asking if there's something I can do to help you.

547
00:36:13,620 --> 00:36:15,190
- Dragonglass? - Yes.

548
00:36:15,190 --> 00:36:17,720
Volcanic glass, obsidian.

549
00:36:17,720 --> 00:36:19,630
He says you have a tremendous amount of it here.

550
00:36:19,630 --> 00:36:21,320
Why are we talking about glass?

551
00:36:21,560 --> 00:36:23,520
We just lost two of our allies.

552
00:36:23,520 --> 00:36:27,210
Which is why I was speaking to Jon Snow, a potential ally.

553
00:36:29,310 --> 00:36:32,910
And what does the King in the North want with dragonglass?

554
00:36:32,970 --> 00:36:35,260
Apparently, it can be turned into weapons

555
00:36:35,260 --> 00:36:37,990
that kill white walkers and their foot soldiers.

556
00:36:38,160 --> 00:36:39,740
Or stop them.

557
00:36:40,450 --> 00:36:41,450
Destroy them.

558
00:36:41,750 --> 00:36:43,730
Unsure about the nomenclature.

559
00:36:45,510 --> 00:36:48,380
And what do you think about this Army of the Dead

560
00:36:48,570 --> 00:36:51,250
and white walkers and Night Kings?

561
00:36:51,250 --> 00:36:54,190
I'd very much like to believe that Jon Snow is wrong.

562
00:36:54,340 --> 00:36:57,110
But a wise man once said that you should never believe a thing

563
00:36:57,110 --> 00:36:59,280
simply because you want to believe it.

564
00:37:02,260 --> 00:37:03,930
Which wise man said this?

565
00:37:05,610 --> 00:37:06,820
I don't remember.

566
00:37:07,460 --> 00:37:10,610
Are you trying to present your own statements as ancient wisdom?

567
00:37:12,150 --> 00:37:13,560
I would never do that.

568
00:37:14,420 --> 00:37:15,330
To you.

569
00:37:17,370 --> 00:37:20,380
The reason I believe Jon Snow is because he's here.

570
00:37:20,810 --> 00:37:23,130
All of his advisors would have told him not to come.

571
00:37:23,130 --> 00:37:24,940
I would have told him not to come.

572
00:37:25,200 --> 00:37:26,580
And he's here anyway.

573
00:37:27,670 --> 00:37:29,250
You don't have to believe him.

574
00:37:29,950 --> 00:37:31,860
Let him mine the dragonglass.

575
00:37:32,130 --> 00:37:33,700
If he's wrong, it's worthless.

576
00:37:33,700 --> 00:37:35,390
You didn't even know it was here.

577
00:37:35,720 --> 00:37:36,860
It's nothing to you.

578
00:37:38,360 --> 00:37:41,340
Give him something by giving him nothing.

579
00:37:41,620 --> 00:37:44,060
Take a step toward a more productive relationship

580
00:37:44,060 --> 00:37:45,500
with a possible ally.

581
00:37:46,890 --> 00:37:49,670
Keep him occupied while we focus on the task at hand

582
00:37:50,290 --> 00:37:51,520
Casterly Rock.

583
00:37:52,910 --> 00:37:54,590
What was that Ser Davos said

584
00:37:54,740 --> 00:37:58,370
about taking a knife in the heart for his people?

585
00:37:58,680 --> 00:37:59,830
Did you notice that?

586
00:38:00,550 --> 00:38:02,610
You must allow them their flights of fancy.

587
00:38:03,180 --> 00:38:04,580
It's dreary in the North.

588
00:38:20,880 --> 00:38:22,190
Amazing thing to see.

589
00:38:23,950 --> 00:38:26,880
I named them for my brothers, Viserys and Rhaegar.

590
00:38:28,230 --> 00:38:29,420
They're both gone now.

591
00:38:31,860 --> 00:38:33,500
You lost two brothers as well.

592
00:38:36,670 --> 00:38:39,500
People thought dragons were gone forever, but here they are.

593
00:38:41,200 --> 00:38:44,050
Perhaps we should all be examining what we think we know.

594
00:38:49,890 --> 00:38:51,370
You've been talking to Tyrion.

595
00:38:52,100 --> 00:38:53,390
He is my Hand.

596
00:38:54,930 --> 00:38:57,950
- He enjoys talking. - We all enjoy what we're good at.

597
00:38:59,070 --> 00:39:00,100
I don't.

598
00:39:05,570 --> 00:39:08,430
You know I'm not going to let Cersei stay on the Iron Throne.

599
00:39:08,430 --> 00:39:09,690
I never expected that you would.

600
00:39:09,690 --> 00:39:10,610
And I haven't changed my mind

601
00:39:10,610 --> 00:39:13,020
about which kingdoms belong to that throne.

602
00:39:13,020 --> 00:39:14,140
I haven't either.

603
00:39:24,610 --> 00:39:25,570
I will allow you to mine

604
00:39:25,570 --> 00:39:28,040
the dragonglass and forge weapons from it.

605
00:39:28,390 --> 00:39:31,160
Any resources or men you need, I will provide for you.

606
00:39:34,720 --> 00:39:35,510
Thank you.

607
00:39:42,530 --> 00:39:43,630
So you believe me, then,

608
00:39:43,630 --> 00:39:45,910
about the Night King and the Army of the Dead?

609
00:39:49,270 --> 00:39:51,230
You'd better get to work, Jon Snow.

610
00:40:16,470 --> 00:40:18,100
How much do we have?

611
00:40:18,170 --> 00:40:20,240
4,000 bushels, my lady.

612
00:40:20,300 --> 00:40:21,320
What does that mean?

613
00:40:21,450 --> 00:40:23,430
For the current occupants of the castle,

614
00:40:23,430 --> 00:40:26,470
it's enough food for a year, perhaps more.

615
00:40:27,250 --> 00:40:30,250
And what's the longest winter in the past hundred years?

616
00:40:30,610 --> 00:40:33,110
Uh, I'm not entirely certain.

617
00:40:33,110 --> 00:40:35,340
I'll check Maester Luwin's records.

618
00:40:35,340 --> 00:40:37,620
He kept a copy of every raven scroll.

619
00:40:38,450 --> 00:40:40,680
You're telling me we don't have enough food,

620
00:40:40,680 --> 00:40:41,880
especially not if the armies

621
00:40:41,880 --> 00:40:44,380
of the North come back to defend Winterfell?

622
00:40:44,840 --> 00:40:47,290
No, my lady, most likely not.

623
00:40:47,290 --> 00:40:49,440
Then we must prepare for that eventuality.

624
00:40:49,720 --> 00:40:51,260
Whatever direction the threat comes from,

625
00:40:51,260 --> 00:40:53,000
this is the best place to be.

626
00:40:53,900 --> 00:40:55,670
We need to start building up our grain stores

627
00:40:55,670 --> 00:40:58,420
with regular shipments from every keep in the North.

628
00:40:58,480 --> 00:41:00,510
If we don't use it by winter's end, we'll give it back to them.

629
00:41:00,510 --> 00:41:02,880
But if the entire North has to flee to Winterfell,

630
00:41:02,880 --> 00:41:04,660
they won't have enough time to bring

631
00:41:04,660 --> 00:41:06,610
wagonloads of grain with them.

632
00:41:06,610 --> 00:41:08,120
Very wise, my lady.

633
00:41:08,120 --> 00:41:09,760
Maester Wolkan, you'll see to it?

634
00:41:13,740 --> 00:41:15,810
Are they covering those breastplates in leather?

635
00:41:16,130 --> 00:41:17,650
No, my lady.

636
00:41:17,880 --> 00:41:20,590
Well, shouldn't they be? Once the real cold comes?

637
00:41:20,590 --> 00:41:21,880
They should, indeed.

638
00:41:22,050 --> 00:41:23,340
Pardon me, my lady.

639
00:41:24,390 --> 00:41:26,490
You there, why isn't there leather on these?

640
00:41:28,790 --> 00:41:30,250
Command suits you.

641
00:41:32,460 --> 00:41:34,510
The Northerners are all facing north,

642
00:41:34,510 --> 00:41:36,420
worried about the threat from beyond the Wall.

643
00:41:36,430 --> 00:41:37,700
So they should be.

644
00:41:38,020 --> 00:41:40,420
I know Cersei better than anyone here.

645
00:41:42,670 --> 00:41:45,140
You don't know Cersei better than anyone here.

646
00:41:46,770 --> 00:41:48,110
That the woman who murdered my mother,

647
00:41:48,110 --> 00:41:50,200
father, and brother is dangerous?

648
00:41:50,200 --> 00:41:51,970
Thank you for your wise counsel.

649
00:41:53,520 --> 00:41:55,200
One of two things will happen,

650
00:41:55,820 --> 00:41:57,850
either the dead will defeat the living,

651
00:41:57,850 --> 00:41:59,030
in which case...

652
00:42:00,170 --> 00:42:01,760
all our troubles come to an end,

653
00:42:01,990 --> 00:42:04,280
or life will win out.

654
00:42:05,140 --> 00:42:06,280
And what then?

655
00:42:07,440 --> 00:42:10,550
Don't fight in the North or the South.

656
00:42:12,050 --> 00:42:16,760
Fight every battle, everywhere, always, in your mind.

657
00:42:18,840 --> 00:42:20,280
Everyone is your enemy,

658
00:42:20,620 --> 00:42:22,280
everyone is your friend,

659
00:42:23,610 --> 00:42:28,230
every possible series of events is happening all at once.

660
00:42:28,470 --> 00:42:31,230
Live that way and nothing will surprise you.

661
00:42:32,130 --> 00:42:33,740
Everything that happens will be something

662
00:42:33,740 --> 00:42:35,440
that you've seen before.

663
00:42:38,340 --> 00:42:40,620
Lady Sansa, at the gate.

664
00:43:13,500 --> 00:43:14,800
Hello, Sansa.

665
00:43:35,360 --> 00:43:36,840
I wish Jon were here.

666
00:43:37,570 --> 00:43:40,700
Yes, I need to speak to him.

667
00:43:44,750 --> 00:43:47,580
You're Father's last living trueborn son.

668
00:43:49,590 --> 00:43:51,280
You're Lord of Winterfell now.

669
00:43:52,120 --> 00:43:54,130
I can never be Lord of Winterfell.

670
00:43:55,270 --> 00:43:57,060
I can never be lord of anything.

671
00:43:57,110 --> 00:43:58,480
I'm the Three-Eyed Raven.

672
00:44:00,440 --> 00:44:02,100
I don't know what that means.

673
00:44:02,850 --> 00:44:04,530
It's difficult to explain.

674
00:44:04,630 --> 00:44:06,650
Try. Please, for me.

675
00:44:08,360 --> 00:44:09,950
It means I can see everything.

676
00:44:11,580 --> 00:44:13,960
Everything that's ever happened to everyone.

677
00:44:14,190 --> 00:44:16,120
Everything that's happening right now.

678
00:44:16,850 --> 00:44:20,430
It's all pieces now, fragments.

679
00:44:21,660 --> 00:44:23,360
I need to learn to see better.

680
00:44:24,020 --> 00:44:25,840
When the Long Night comes again,

681
00:44:27,110 --> 00:44:28,290
I need to be ready.

682
00:44:31,940 --> 00:44:34,360
How do you know all this?

683
00:44:34,360 --> 00:44:35,890
The Three-Eyed Raven taught me.

684
00:44:35,950 --> 00:44:38,010
I thought you were the Three-Eyed Raven.

685
00:44:38,230 --> 00:44:40,420
I told you it's difficult to explain.

686
00:44:43,580 --> 00:44:44,150
Bran--

687
00:44:44,150 --> 00:44:45,900
I'm sorry for all that's happened to you.

688
00:44:47,190 --> 00:44:50,360
I'm sorry it had to happen here in our home.

689
00:44:55,890 --> 00:44:57,640
It was so beautiful that night.

690
00:44:59,920 --> 00:45:03,820
Snow falling, just like now.

691
00:45:07,320 --> 00:45:08,910
And you were so beautiful...

692
00:45:11,010 --> 00:45:12,670
in your white wedding dress.

693
00:45:16,650 --> 00:45:18,360
I have to go back inside, Bran.

694
00:45:19,740 --> 00:45:21,000
I'll stay a bit longer.

695
00:45:52,390 --> 00:45:53,620
Does it hurt?

696
00:45:54,280 --> 00:45:57,260
A bit. Less than before.

697
00:45:59,200 --> 00:46:01,780
The infection no longer appears to be active.

698
00:46:03,030 --> 00:46:04,190
Unusual.

699
00:46:04,940 --> 00:46:05,990
Unlikely.

700
00:46:06,740 --> 00:46:09,620
One could almost be forgiven for thinking that the entire

701
00:46:09,620 --> 00:46:12,680
upper layer of diseased skin was debrided

702
00:46:12,950 --> 00:46:16,520
and the underlying region treated with some sort of unguent.

703
00:46:17,070 --> 00:46:18,700
Don't know anything about that.

704
00:46:19,860 --> 00:46:21,830
I just started feeling better.

705
00:46:22,150 --> 00:46:24,840
I assumed it was the rest that did it.

706
00:46:27,430 --> 00:46:28,620
And the climate.

707
00:46:30,030 --> 00:46:31,170
The climate.

708
00:46:32,470 --> 00:46:33,630
You're free to go, ser.

709
00:46:33,840 --> 00:46:36,000
This chamber is needed for the infectious,

710
00:46:36,000 --> 00:46:37,390
which you are no longer.

711
00:46:37,600 --> 00:46:40,890
Tarly, I'd like to speak with you in my study this evening.

712
00:46:44,030 --> 00:46:45,090
How bad is it?

713
00:46:46,940 --> 00:46:48,730
Suppose I'll find out this evening.

714
00:46:53,500 --> 00:46:54,490
Where will you go?

715
00:46:56,210 --> 00:46:59,660
I surrendered to this sickness the moment I first saw it.

716
00:47:01,340 --> 00:47:02,790
I knew it would kill me

717
00:47:04,170 --> 00:47:06,230
or I'd kill myself before it could.

718
00:47:06,920 --> 00:47:09,800
Daenerys Stormborn convinced me otherwise.

719
00:47:10,140 --> 00:47:12,240
The only place for me is back with her.

720
00:47:13,610 --> 00:47:15,120
I owe her my life.

721
00:47:16,060 --> 00:47:18,610
Her and you.

722
00:47:21,030 --> 00:47:23,020
Your father saved me more than once.

723
00:47:23,350 --> 00:47:24,710
It's the least I could do.

724
00:47:26,650 --> 00:47:28,760
Perhaps our paths will cross again.

725
00:47:29,760 --> 00:47:30,850
I hope they do.

726
00:47:58,530 --> 00:48:00,630
- You treated him? - Yes.

727
00:48:01,880 --> 00:48:03,400
Who told you to treat him?

728
00:48:04,710 --> 00:48:05,700
No one.

729
00:48:05,700 --> 00:48:09,220
Who forbade you, or anyone, to attempt to treat him?

730
00:48:09,440 --> 00:48:11,710
I seem to remember you.

731
00:48:11,710 --> 00:48:14,510
- But you treated him anyway? - I did, yes.

732
00:48:16,210 --> 00:48:19,520
I forbade it because it is dangerous and rarely successful,

733
00:48:19,520 --> 00:48:21,510
especially on someone of that age.

734
00:48:21,720 --> 00:48:24,190
You could have infected yourself and others.

735
00:48:24,330 --> 00:48:27,360
You could have devastated the entire Citadel.

736
00:48:29,610 --> 00:48:30,770
But you didn't.

737
00:48:31,630 --> 00:48:34,530
It's a meticulous, difficult procedure.

738
00:48:34,530 --> 00:48:37,380
Many maesters whose chains are heavy with healing links

739
00:48:37,380 --> 00:48:39,380
have attempted it and failed.

740
00:48:40,200 --> 00:48:41,430
Yet you succeeded.

741
00:48:42,650 --> 00:48:43,520
How?

742
00:48:45,150 --> 00:48:48,400
I read the books and followed the instructions.

743
00:48:58,830 --> 00:49:01,000
That man is alive because of you.

744
00:49:03,440 --> 00:49:04,940
You should be proud.

745
00:49:08,090 --> 00:49:10,010
Thank you, Archmaester.

746
00:49:10,620 --> 00:49:11,690
Come here.

747
00:49:15,610 --> 00:49:19,040
All these manuscripts and scrolls are rotting away.

748
00:49:20,220 --> 00:49:22,000
I need you to make copies of them.

749
00:49:26,430 --> 00:49:28,160
You were expecting a reward.

750
00:49:29,950 --> 00:49:34,230
Your reward is not being immediately expelled from the Citadel.

751
00:49:35,120 --> 00:49:36,600
You'd better get started.

752
00:49:37,150 --> 00:49:38,700
And careful of the paper mites.

753
00:49:38,700 --> 00:49:40,270
They like flesh as well.

754
00:49:47,290 --> 00:49:50,780
We need to find Euron Greyjoy's fleet and sink it.

755
00:49:50,780 --> 00:49:54,260
Your Grace, he's already destroyed a good portion of our fleet.

756
00:49:54,260 --> 00:49:55,600
To send our remaining ships after him--

757
00:49:55,600 --> 00:49:58,440
I'm not talking about sending our ships after him.

758
00:50:02,070 --> 00:50:03,800
Would you have to go yourself?

759
00:50:03,850 --> 00:50:05,560
Euron's ships could be anywhere

760
00:50:05,570 --> 00:50:07,380
or in more than one place.

761
00:50:07,790 --> 00:50:10,000
You'd be flying around the open seas alone

762
00:50:10,000 --> 00:50:11,060
for who knows how long.

763
00:50:11,060 --> 00:50:12,250
I wouldn't be alone.

764
00:50:12,690 --> 00:50:15,750
I would have Drogon, Viserion, and Rhaegal.

765
00:50:15,750 --> 00:50:17,060
What can anyone do to them?

766
00:50:17,060 --> 00:50:18,960
They can still do something to you.

767
00:50:19,150 --> 00:50:20,780
It only takes one arrow.

768
00:50:20,980 --> 00:50:23,260
It's too great a risk. You're too important.

769
00:50:25,670 --> 00:50:27,470
What about Casterly Rock?

770
00:50:27,810 --> 00:50:29,670
The Unsullied will be there soon.

771
00:50:29,930 --> 00:50:31,340
And what will they face?

772
00:50:33,300 --> 00:50:35,120
A difficult situation.

773
00:50:35,780 --> 00:50:37,040
They know we're coming.

774
00:50:37,040 --> 00:50:40,220
Yes. Cersei believes my sole purpose in life

775
00:50:40,220 --> 00:50:42,030
is to destroy House Lannister.

776
00:50:42,600 --> 00:50:43,870
She will be ready.

777
00:50:47,630 --> 00:50:50,570
- No one has ever taken the Rock. - Archers!

778
00:50:50,570 --> 00:50:52,770
The Lannister Army is still the army my father built.

779
00:50:52,770 --> 00:50:54,940
- Come on! - Well-trained and well-provisioned.

780
00:50:54,940 --> 00:50:56,720
10,000 men at least.

781
00:50:56,720 --> 00:50:58,050
They will see us coming.

782
00:51:02,480 --> 00:51:03,550
They will be ready.

783
00:51:07,420 --> 00:51:10,000
Draw! Loose! Loose!

784
00:51:11,560 --> 00:51:14,460
The gates of Casterly Rock are impregnable.

785
00:51:22,670 --> 00:51:24,650
The fight up the walls will be hard.

786
00:51:24,750 --> 00:51:26,610
We will be at a disadvantage.

787
00:51:28,050 --> 00:51:29,710
Many men will die.

788
00:51:31,380 --> 00:51:33,000
Just as my father said they would.

789
00:51:35,820 --> 00:51:37,750
Interesting thing about my father--

790
00:51:38,260 --> 00:51:40,200
he built our house up from near ruin.

791
00:51:40,280 --> 00:51:43,710
He built our army, he built Casterly Rock as we know it,

792
00:51:44,450 --> 00:51:46,550
but he didn't build the sewers.

793
00:51:46,960 --> 00:51:48,280
That was beneath him,

794
00:51:48,540 --> 00:51:51,250
so he gave the job to the lowest person he could find--

795
00:51:51,960 --> 00:51:52,920
me.

796
00:51:53,150 --> 00:51:54,710
He was right, I was low.

797
00:51:54,710 --> 00:51:56,910
The company I kept, low.

798
00:51:56,960 --> 00:51:58,100
Women, mostly.

799
00:51:58,300 --> 00:52:00,130
They weren't welcome at the Rock.

800
00:52:00,190 --> 00:52:02,130
Father disapproved of that sort of behavior.

801
00:52:02,240 --> 00:52:03,760
Couldn't walk them through the front gates,

802
00:52:03,760 --> 00:52:05,510
I couldn't have them in my chambers,

803
00:52:05,510 --> 00:52:08,240
so in the process of building the sewers,

804
00:52:08,650 --> 00:52:10,670
I threw in something for myself.

805
00:52:12,530 --> 00:52:14,580
It was a passage that began

806
00:52:14,580 --> 00:52:16,150
in an out of the way cove by the sea

807
00:52:16,150 --> 00:52:18,550
and ended beneath one of the main guard towers.

808
00:52:19,910 --> 00:52:22,980
No better place for low pursuits than beneath the ground.

809
00:52:24,830 --> 00:52:27,880
Casterly Rock is an impregnable fortress.

810
00:52:30,600 --> 00:52:32,460
But as a good friend of mine once said,

811
00:52:34,340 --> 00:52:38,100
"Give me 10 good men and I'll impregnate the bitch."

812
00:52:43,560 --> 00:52:45,120
And so it begins.

813
00:52:51,650 --> 00:52:54,310
They will face the bulk of the Lannister forces.

814
00:52:54,620 --> 00:52:55,820
They will be outnumbered.

815
00:52:56,270 --> 00:52:58,620
They will have less armor and fewer weapons.

816
00:53:03,650 --> 00:53:06,980
But my sister's armies fight for her out of fear.

817
00:53:07,510 --> 00:53:10,370
The Unsullied will be fighting for something greater.

818
00:53:10,370 --> 00:53:12,160
They will be fighting for freedom

819
00:53:12,200 --> 00:53:14,110
and the person who gave it to them.

820
00:53:14,110 --> 00:53:15,720
They will be fighting for you.

821
00:53:16,580 --> 00:53:19,020
And that is why they will triumph.

822
00:54:06,210 --> 00:54:07,150
Where are they?!

823
00:54:07,650 --> 00:54:09,670
Where are the rest of the Lannisters?

824
00:55:38,430 --> 00:55:41,230
- It's done. - It is.

825
00:55:42,570 --> 00:55:46,970
And now the rains weep o'er our halls.

826
00:55:49,480 --> 00:55:50,770
Did we fight well?

827
00:55:51,060 --> 00:55:53,650
Uh, as well as could be expected.

828
00:55:53,710 --> 00:55:55,410
It was never our forte.

829
00:55:55,720 --> 00:55:57,910
Golden roses, indeed.

830
00:56:00,010 --> 00:56:01,780
Your brother and his new queen

831
00:56:01,780 --> 00:56:04,780
thought you would be defending Casterly Rock.

832
00:56:04,790 --> 00:56:07,850
The truth is Casterly Rock isn't worth much anymore.

833
00:56:08,290 --> 00:56:09,560
Well, it is to me,

834
00:56:09,560 --> 00:56:11,770
but my fond childhood memories

835
00:56:11,770 --> 00:56:13,550
won't keep Cersei on the throne.

836
00:56:13,550 --> 00:56:15,640
So you just let them take it?

837
00:56:15,640 --> 00:56:17,860
For now. They won't be able to hold it.

838
00:56:17,860 --> 00:56:20,210
Euron Greyjoy's navy burned their ships,

839
00:56:20,210 --> 00:56:22,160
we emptied the larders before we left.

840
00:56:22,160 --> 00:56:24,200
Eventually, they'll be forced to abandon their position

841
00:56:24,200 --> 00:56:27,490
and march all the way across Westeros.

842
00:56:28,030 --> 00:56:31,030
And you took your army, your real army,

843
00:56:31,190 --> 00:56:32,940
and went where they weren't.

844
00:56:32,940 --> 00:56:35,850
As Robb Stark did to me at Whispering Wood.

845
00:56:36,330 --> 00:56:38,230
There are always lessons in failures.

846
00:56:38,230 --> 00:56:42,170
Yes. You must be very wise by now.

847
00:56:43,160 --> 00:56:45,730
My father always said I was a slow learner.

848
00:56:46,050 --> 00:56:47,620
If he was so clever,

849
00:56:47,720 --> 00:56:49,470
why didn't he take Highgarden

850
00:56:49,470 --> 00:56:52,760
the moment your gold mines ran dry?

851
00:56:54,190 --> 00:56:58,090
I suppose I'll be able to ask him myself soon enough.

852
00:56:58,670 --> 00:57:02,300
No more learning from my mistakes, eh?

853
00:57:04,210 --> 00:57:05,600
How will you do it?

854
00:57:06,960 --> 00:57:08,230
With that sword?

855
00:57:09,160 --> 00:57:11,200
That was Joffrey's sword, wasn't it?

856
00:57:11,520 --> 00:57:13,250
Not that he ever used it.

857
00:57:13,980 --> 00:57:15,340
What did he call it?

858
00:57:17,060 --> 00:57:18,400
Widow's Wail.

859
00:57:19,470 --> 00:57:21,440
He really was a cunt, wasn't he?

860
00:57:23,660 --> 00:57:28,410
I did unspeakable things to protect my family.

861
00:57:28,840 --> 00:57:32,170
Or watched them being done on my orders.

862
00:57:32,910 --> 00:57:35,330
I never lost a night's sleep over them.

863
00:57:35,950 --> 00:57:37,350
They were necessary.

864
00:57:37,950 --> 00:57:40,020
And whatever I imagined necessary

865
00:57:40,030 --> 00:57:43,450
for the safety of House Tyrell, I did.

866
00:57:44,490 --> 00:57:48,890
But your sister has done things...

867
00:57:50,100 --> 00:57:52,830
I was incapable of imagining.

868
00:57:53,140 --> 00:57:55,170
That was my prize mistake--

869
00:57:55,360 --> 00:57:57,740
a failure of imagination.

870
00:57:59,280 --> 00:58:01,640
She's a monster, you do know that?

871
00:58:02,130 --> 00:58:03,630
To you, I'm sure.

872
00:58:03,770 --> 00:58:04,980
To others as well.

873
00:58:05,910 --> 00:58:09,270
But after we've won and there's no one left to oppose us,

874
00:58:09,420 --> 00:58:13,050
when people are living peacefully in the world she built,

875
00:58:13,740 --> 00:58:14,740
do you really think they'll

876
00:58:14,740 --> 00:58:17,100
wring their hands over the way she built it?

877
00:58:19,850 --> 00:58:20,920
You love her.

878
00:58:21,830 --> 00:58:23,490
You really do love her.

879
00:58:23,700 --> 00:58:25,350
You poor fool.

880
00:58:26,060 --> 00:58:27,600
She'll be the end of you.

881
00:58:28,400 --> 00:58:29,380
Possibly.

882
00:58:31,320 --> 00:58:32,220
Not much to be gained

883
00:58:32,220 --> 00:58:34,330
from discussing it with you, though, is there?

884
00:58:34,340 --> 00:58:37,060
What better person to discuss it with?

885
00:58:37,060 --> 00:58:38,990
What better guarantee could you have

886
00:58:38,990 --> 00:58:42,600
that the things you say will never leave this room?

887
00:58:43,940 --> 00:58:45,620
But perhaps you're right.

888
00:58:45,970 --> 00:58:47,340
If she's driven you this far,

889
00:58:47,340 --> 00:58:50,160
it's gone beyond your control.

890
00:58:51,290 --> 00:58:52,180
Yes.

891
00:58:53,300 --> 00:58:54,320
It has.

892
00:58:55,590 --> 00:58:57,580
She's a disease.

893
00:58:57,840 --> 00:59:00,550
I regret my role in spreading it.

894
00:59:00,770 --> 00:59:02,290
You will, too.

895
00:59:02,720 --> 00:59:04,040
I think we're done here.

896
00:59:07,440 --> 00:59:08,700
How will it happen?

897
00:59:10,080 --> 00:59:12,460
Cersei had several ideas.

898
00:59:12,470 --> 00:59:13,600
Whipping you through the streets

899
00:59:13,600 --> 00:59:15,970
and beheading you in front of the Red Keep.

900
00:59:16,350 --> 00:59:17,580
Flaying you alive and

901
00:59:17,580 --> 00:59:20,170
hanging you from the walls of King's Landing.

902
00:59:23,090 --> 00:59:24,680
I talked her out of those.

903
00:59:42,300 --> 00:59:43,560
Will there be pain?

904
00:59:43,740 --> 00:59:45,550
No. I made sure of that.

905
00:59:46,170 --> 00:59:47,130
That's good.

906
01:00:00,470 --> 01:00:02,440
I'd hate to die like your son.

907
01:00:03,370 --> 01:00:04,910
Clawing at my neck,

908
01:00:04,990 --> 01:00:07,910
foam and bile spilling from my mouth,

909
01:00:07,910 --> 01:00:11,380
eyes bloodred, skin purple.

910
01:00:11,960 --> 01:00:14,050
Must have been horrible for you,

911
01:00:14,080 --> 01:00:17,300
as a Kingsguard, as a father.

912
01:00:17,730 --> 01:00:19,650
It was horrible enough for me.

913
01:00:20,100 --> 01:00:22,020
A shocking scene.

914
01:00:22,760 --> 01:00:25,490
Not at all what I intended.

915
01:00:27,730 --> 01:00:32,080
You see, I had never seen the poison work before.

916
01:00:37,180 --> 01:00:38,390
Tell Cersei.

917
01:00:39,280 --> 01:00:41,310
I want her to know it was me.

918
01:02:25,940 --> 01:02:27,400
My only venture at this moment

919
01:02:27,400 --> 01:02:29,950
is reestablishing control over this continent

920
01:02:29,950 --> 01:02:31,540
and every person on it.

